# A finger held on a word of River.epub looks the word up. The simulator has
# no dictionary installed, so the screen says so and shows the command that
# adds one. From there the word is highlighted and given a note, and both are
# still in the book after a restart.
wait-for River
tap River
wait-for Marker 1
# A hold is a finger kept down, which the tap steps cannot do, so it is
# replayed as the panel's own touch records: down on "move" in the first
# paragraph, most of a second, then up.
input touch 3 47 0;3 57 9;3 53 520;3 54 771;0 0 0
wait 700
input touch 3 57 -1;0 0 0
wait-for No dictionary on this reader has this word.
expect move
expect kobo dict install
shot books-word
tap Highlight
wait-for Marker 1
expect-missing No dictionary
shot books-word-highlighted
# Held again, the same word offers to take its highlight off, and a note.
input touch 3 47 0;3 57 9;3 53 520;3 54 771;0 0 0
wait 700
input touch 3 57 -1;0 0 0
wait-for Remove highlight
tap Add note
wait-for-id kb.enter
shot books-word-note
type seen at dusk
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for Marker 1
# The note is listed with its word, and the row goes back to the page.
tap-id reader-controls
wait-for Page 1 of
tap-id reader-highlights
wait-for Highlights and notes
expect move: seen at dusk
shot books-word-notes
tap move: seen at dusk
wait-for Marker 1
# Back from a definition goes back to the page, not out of the book.
input touch 3 47 0;3 57 9;3 53 520;3 54 771;0 0 0
wait 700
input touch 3 57 -1;0 0 0
wait-for Edit note
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Marker 1
expect-missing Continue reading
# The highlight and its note come back after a restart.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Continue reading
restart
wait-for Continue reading
tap Continue reading
wait-for Marker 1
tap-id reader-controls
wait-for Page 1 of
tap-id reader-highlights
wait-for Highlights and notes
expect move: seen at dusk
